    "metaDescription": "Lakefront 3-bed, 3-bath single-level home with two primary suites in the gated Biltmore community of Village on the Lakes, Phoenix 85016, listed at $1,795,000.",
    "content": "<h2>Lakefront Living in the Heart of the Biltmore</h2>\n<p>Few addresses in Phoenix carry the cachet of the Arizona Biltmore, and fewer still put you on the water. <strong>3106 E Georgia Avenue</strong> sits on a premium lot inside the gated community of <strong>Village on the Lakes at the Arizona Biltmore Estates</strong>, where lake, golf course and mountain views come with the territory. Listed at <strong>$1,795,000</strong>, this single-level home offers <strong>3 bedrooms, 3 bathrooms and 2,251 square feet</strong>, plus a 2-car garage, in one of the most established luxury enclaves in the 85016 zip code.</p>\n<p>If you want the Biltmore lifestyle without stairs, without a sprawling yard to maintain, and with a view you won't get tired of, this is a listing worth seeing in person.</p>\n\n<h2>A Split Floor Plan With Two Primary Suites</h2>\n<p>The layout is the headline here. A <strong>split floor plan with two primary suites</strong> is rare at this size, and it opens up options that a standard plan can't match: multigenerational living, long-term guests, a live-in caregiver, or simply two people who each want their own retreat. A third bedroom and third bathroom round out the plan, giving you flexibility for an office, a guest room or a hobby space.</p>\n<p>Highlights from the MLS listing include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Single-level living</strong> with no interior stairs to navigate</li>\n<li><strong>Two primary suites</strong>, each with a full bath, plus double vanity and a separate shower and tub</li>\n<li><strong>Updated kitchen</strong> with upgraded appliances, granite counters, an eat-in area and views of the side courtyard</li>\n<li><strong>Living room with beamed ceilings and a fireplace</strong>, where the lake views take center stage</li>\n<li>A light, neutral palette that makes it easy to move in and add your own finishes</li>\n<li>Natural gas heating, central air and a <strong>2-car garage</strong></li>\n<li>Built in <strong>1980</strong> within a mature, gated Biltmore community</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>The Biltmore Neighborhood</h2>\n<p>The Arizona Biltmore area is one of Phoenix's most recognizable addresses. Residents are minutes from <strong>Biltmore Fashion Park</strong> and the restaurants and boutiques along Camelback Road, and the historic Arizona Biltmore resort and its golf courses are close by. The neighborhood also sits between the city's major job centers: Camelback Corridor offices, Downtown Phoenix and Old Town Scottsdale are all a short drive away.</p>\n<p>Getting around is easy too. The listing notes <strong>easy access to SR 51</strong>, which connects quickly to the Loop 101, the I-10 and Sky Harbor International Airport. Piestewa Peak and the Phoenix Mountains Preserve are nearby for sunrise hikes, so you can have trails and fine dining on the same morning.</p>\n\n<h2>Market Context: Is This a Good Value?</h2>\n<p>At roughly <strong>$797 per square foot</strong>, this home is priced like what it is: a lakefront property inside a gated Biltmore community. Waterfront lots are scarce in central Phoenix, and homes with lake, golf and mountain views in the same frame tend to hold their value well because the supply simply can't grow. Single-level plans with two primary suites also appeal to a wide buyer pool, from downsizers leaving larger estates to second-home buyers who want a lock-and-leave base close to everything.</p>\n<p>Buyers comparing this home with others nearby should look at lot position, view corridors, HOA dues and what the community covers, and the cost of any updates they'd like to make. A careful review of recent sales inside Village on the Lakes and the surrounding Biltmore Estates is the best way to judge where this price sits, and we're happy to put that comparison together for you.</p>\n\n<h2>Buy With Attorney and Paralegal Oversight</h2>\n<p>A purchase at this price point deserves more than a standard transaction. At <strong>Camelback Home Group</strong>, every deal is supported by <strong>attorney and paralegal oversight</strong> from contract to closing. That means a close review of the purchase contract, HOA documents, CC&amp;Rs and title commitment, attention to deadlines during the inspection period, and someone in your corner who knows what to look for before you sign. In a gated community with its own rules and assessments, that extra layer of review matters.</p>\n\n<h2>Schedule a Private Showing</h2>\n<p>Want to see the lake views from that living room for yourself? Contact the Camelback Home Group team at <strong>(480) 203-3039</strong> to schedule a private showing of 3106 E Georgia Avenue, request recent comparable sales, or talk through financing and offer strategy. Homes like this don't come up often in the Biltmore, so it pays to move early.</p>"
