    "excerpt": "An updated 3-bedroom, 2.5-bath home in a gated Fountain Hills community with owned solar, HVAC from 2023, and a backyard with a newly resurfaced heated PebbleTec pool, a gazebo and an outdoor fireplace. Listed at $1,300,000 in Westridge Village.",
    "metaDescription": "Explore 10810 N Rosemont Court in Fountain Hills, AZ: an updated, gated 3-bed, 2.5-bath, 2,632 sq ft home with owned solar and a heated pool, listed at $1.3M.",
    "content": "<h2>Updated and Ready to Move In, in Westridge Village</h2>\n<p>10810 N Rosemont Court is in a <strong>gated community</strong> in Fountain Hills, in the Westridge Village subdivision. It is listed at <strong>$1,300,000</strong>. The single-level ranch-style home was built in 2000 and has <strong>3 bedrooms</strong>, <strong>2.5 bathrooms</strong>, about <strong>2,632 square feet</strong>, and a <strong>3-car garage</strong>. The sellers have already done the updates most buyers would put on a list for the first few years, so the home is ready to move into.</p>\n<h2>Upgrades That Matter</h2>\n<p>Many updated homes only have new surfaces. This one also has updates to systems that affect what it costs to own:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Owned solar</strong>, not leased, so no lease transfer and no monthly solar payment</li>\n<li><strong>Newer HVAC units (2023)</strong> with programmable thermostats and ceiling fans</li>\n<li>Fresh <strong>interior and exterior paint</strong> and updated lighting</li>\n<li>Refinished cabinetry and <strong>new countertops</strong></li>\n<li>Updated appliances and a <strong>gas cooktop</strong> in the kitchen</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Owned solar plus new air conditioning should keep summer utility bills well below those of comparable homes. Buyers will still want to review the solar system's age, production history, and warranty during inspection.</p>\n<h2>Interior Layout</h2>\n<p>The kitchen has plenty of cabinet storage and opens to the family room, which has a <strong>gas fireplace</strong> and a <strong>custom built-in workspace</strong>, a useful setup for remote work. The <strong>primary suite</strong> opens directly to the patio, has hand-scraped wood floors and custom built-in cabinetry, and has a fully updated bathroom. The two other bedrooms work well for guests, family, or a hobby room, and the half bath serves visitors.</p>\n<h2>A Backyard Built for Arizona Living</h2>\n<p>The backyard is the best part of the house:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A <strong>newly resurfaced PebbleTec pool</strong>, <strong>heated</strong> so you can swim most of the year</li>\n<li>A new <strong>gazebo</strong> for shaded lounging or outdoor dining</li>\n<li>An <strong>outdoor fireplace</strong> for cool desert evenings</li>\n<li><strong>Electric exterior shades</strong> that cut afternoon sun and glare</li>\n<li>Freshly refreshed landscaping</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Why Fountain Hills</h2>\n<p>Fountain Hills is a small town tucked against the McDowell Mountains, just east of Scottsdale. It feels quieter and more scenic than most of the Valley. The town is known for its famous fountain in Fountain Park, which shoots water hundreds of feet into the air, and it is a designated <strong>International Dark Sky Community</strong>, so the night skies are among the clearest in the metro area.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hiking and biking in <strong>McDowell Mountain Regional Park</strong> and on the town's own trails</li>\n<li>Golf at FireRock, SunRidge Canyon, and nearby courses</li>\n<li>A walkable Avenue of the Fountains with local restaurants, shops, and seasonal festivals</li>\n<li>About 20 to 25 minutes to Old Town Scottsdale and the Scottsdale Airpark</li>\n<li>Close to the Verde River, Saguaro Lake, and the Fort McDowell area for outdoor recreation</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Market Context</h2>\n<p>At about $494 per square foot, this home is in the upper-middle part of the Fountain Hills market. Recent listings in town run from under $450,000 for condos and smaller homes to several million for custom estates on the hillsides. A gated location, owned solar, recent mechanical upgrades, and a resort-style backyard are what set this home apart from older, unrenovated homes at lower prices, which may need $75,000 to $150,000 or more in updates to match. Buyers should compare it against recent sales in gated Westridge Village and nearby communities, and look at HOA dues and gate-related costs.</p>\n<h2>Legal Oversight You Can Count On</h2>\n<p><strong>Camelback Home Group</strong> pairs experienced agents with in-house <strong>attorney and paralegal oversight</strong> on every transaction. For a home like this, that means careful review of the solar ownership documents, the HOA and gated-community disclosures, the SPDS, and the inspection and repair negotiations, all aimed at a smooth closing.</p>\n<h2>Schedule Your Private Showing</h2>\n<p>Updated, gated homes with owned solar and a heated pool don't come up often in Fountain Hills. To tour 10810 N Rosemont Court or to ask for a comparative market analysis, call Camelback Home Group at <strong>(480) 203-3039</strong>.</p>"
