    "content": "<h2>Space, Style, and Verrado Living in Buckeye</h2>\n<p>Buyers searching the West Valley for a home with real room to grow will want to take a close look at <strong>4231 N Sentinel Drive</strong> in Buckeye. Set in the master-planned community of <strong>Verrado</strong>, this two-story contemporary home offers <strong>4 bedrooms, 3.5 bathrooms, and a generous 4,020 square feet</strong> of living space, all for a list price of <strong>$850,000</strong>. Built in 2006 and freshly painted, it combines the maturity of an established neighborhood with the upgrades and flexibility today's households are looking for.</p>\n<p>Homes of this size are hard to find in Verrado, especially with a floor plan that includes a den, a bonus room, and two primary-style bedrooms. Whether you are a large family, a multigenerational household, or someone who works from home and needs dedicated space, this property gives you room to live comfortably.</p>\n<h2>Inside the Home</h2>\n<p>The oversized open floor plan is bathed in natural light and designed for both entertaining and everyday living. A mix of tile and carpet flooring, stylish light fixtures, and <strong>pre-wired surround sound</strong> make the main living areas feel polished and ready for movie nights or game-day gatherings. Ceilings of nine feet and higher add to the sense of openness throughout.</p>\n<p>The kitchen is a true centerpiece. Highlights include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Granite countertops</strong> with a mosaic tile backsplash</li>\n<li>Built-in appliances and ample cabinetry</li>\n<li>A large <strong>walk-in pantry</strong> and a <strong>butler's service area</strong> for staging meals and drinks</li>\n<li>A prep island with a breakfast bar, plus an eat-in dining area</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Upstairs, the spacious primary retreat feels like a private suite. It features a <strong>media niche and a wall-mounted fireplace</strong>, an elegant ensuite bathroom with a garden tub, separate shower, and double vanity, and a walk-in closet. A <strong>second main bedroom</strong> with its own full bath is ideal for guests, older children, or extended family who want privacy. An open den or office and a bonus room give you even more flexibility, and could serve as a playroom, gym, or media lounge.</p>\n<p>Outside, a covered patio offers a shaded place to relax and unwind, and the two-car garage provides parking and storage. Electric heating and central air keep the home comfortable year-round.</p>\n<h2>Why Verrado Stands Out</h2>\n<p>Verrado is one of the most recognized master-planned communities in the West Valley, and for good reason. Nestled against the White Tank Mountains, the community was designed around walkable streets, front porches, and a small-town feel. Its <strong>Main Street district</strong> offers local dining, coffee, and shopping, while community events throughout the year bring neighbors together.</p>\n<p>Residents enjoy access to a wide range of <strong>community amenities</strong>, including pools, fitness facilities, parks, sports courts, and miles of walking and biking trails. Golf lovers will appreciate Verrado Golf Club nearby, and outdoor enthusiasts can head to White Tank Mountain Regional Park for hiking and mountain biking within minutes.</p>\n<p>Buckeye itself is one of the fastest-growing cities in the country. Easy access to Interstate 10 makes commuting to the Phoenix metro manageable, and continued investment in retail, healthcare, and employment centers along the I-10 corridor keeps the area's momentum strong.</p>\n<h2>Market Context: Is It a Good Value?</h2>\n<p>At $850,000 and roughly <strong>$211 per square foot</strong>, this home offers a striking amount of space for the price. Newer construction in the West Valley often runs well above that per-square-foot figure, and finding more than 4,000 square feet inside an established, amenity-rich community like Verrado is uncommon. For buyers who prioritize space and lifestyle, this listing presents a compelling value relative to similarly sized homes in Goodyear, Litchfield Park, and other nearby areas.</p>\n<p>Because the home was built in 2006, buyers should plan on a thorough inspection, with special attention to roof, HVAC, and water heater age. That is exactly the kind of due diligence our team helps clients navigate.</p>\n<h2>Buy With Legal Peace of Mind</h2>\n<p>At Camelback Home Group, every transaction includes <strong>attorney and paralegal oversight</strong> at no additional cost. From reviewing the purchase contract and HOA documents to managing inspection negotiations, title review, and closing, our team brings legal precision to every step, so you can focus on finding the right home rather than worrying about the fine print.</p>\n<h2>Schedule Your Showing</h2>\n<p>Large, upgraded homes in Verrado tend to attract strong interest. If <strong>4231 N Sentinel Drive, Buckeye, AZ 85396</strong> sounds like the right fit, now is the time to see it in person. <strong>Call Camelback Home Group at (480) 203-3039</strong> or <a href=\"/#contact\">contact us online</a> to schedule a private showing or ask any questions about this property.</p>"
