    "content": "<h2>A Brand-New Model Home on an Oversized Buckeye Lot</h2>\n<p>Model homes are where builders put their best foot forward, and <strong>24266 W Atlantis Way</strong> in Buckeye is no exception. Built in 2025 by DRH Properties in the <strong>Apache Farms</strong> community, this 4-bedroom, 2-bathroom single-level ranch home served as the builder's showcase model and is now available to its first owner, fully finished and ready to move in. Listed at <strong>$474,990</strong>, it delivers roughly 1,919 square feet of thoughtfully designed living space on what the listing calls a \"HUGE LOT,\" an increasingly rare find in new-construction neighborhoods.</p>\n<p>Buyers of new homes often discover that the base price leaves a long list of items still to purchase. Here, much of that work has already been done. Stainless steel appliances, window blinds, and even the washer and dryer convey with the home, along with the model's upgraded light fixtures, a detail the listing agent specifically calls out.</p>\n\n<h2>Features and Layout</h2>\n<p>The single-story ranch floor plan places all four bedrooms and both bathrooms on one level, making it a smart fit for growing families, multigenerational households, or buyers who simply prefer to avoid stairs. Highlights from the MLS include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>4 bedrooms and 2 full bathrooms</strong> across approximately 1,919 square feet</li>\n<li><strong>Quartz countertops</strong> and a <strong>walk-in pantry</strong> in the kitchen</li>\n<li><strong>9-foot-plus flat ceilings</strong> that make the rooms feel open and airy</li>\n<li><strong>Smart home</strong> technology built in</li>\n<li><strong>Double vanity</strong> in the primary bathroom</li>\n<li><strong>ENERGY STAR qualified</strong> central air conditioning with electric heat, helping keep summer utility bills in check</li>\n<li>Stainless steel appliances, blinds, and washer/dryer included</li>\n<li><strong>2-car garage</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The backyard is the real standout. It already has artificial turf, trees, and rock landscaping, so it is low-maintenance from day one. It is also large enough to add a pool and still leave room to park an RV, boat, or other toys. In new-build communities where lots are typically tight, that kind of outdoor flexibility is a real advantage.</p>\n\n<h2>Living in Buckeye</h2>\n<p>Buckeye is one of the fastest-growing cities in the United States, and it's easy to see why. Located along the I-10 corridor in the West Valley, it offers newer homes, wide-open desert views, and a slower pace of life, while Goodyear, Avondale, and downtown Phoenix remain an easy drive away. Ongoing investment in retail, healthcare, schools, and employment centers along the I-10 and SR-85 corridors continues to bring more everyday conveniences closer to home.</p>\n<p>Outdoor lovers have the Skyline Regional Park trail system, the White Tank Mountains, and Buckeye Hills Recreation Area nearby, and golf, community parks, and youth sports leagues are all part of daily life here. For buyers priced out of the East Valley or central Phoenix, Buckeye offers more house and more land for the money.</p>\n\n<h2>Market Context: Is This a Good Value?</h2>\n<p>At $474,990, this home works out to roughly <strong>$248 per square foot</strong> for brand-new, model-finished construction. That compares favorably with many resale homes across the West Valley that are a decade or more old and still need updating. Model homes usually include upgrades that would cost thousands of dollars to add to a standard build, and this one also includes appliances, window coverings, and finished landscaping. All of those add to what a buyer actually gets for the price.</p>\n<p>Buyers should still review the builder's purchase contract, warranty terms, HOA documents, and any special assessments or community facilities district obligations before committing. In a new-build community, those documents can significantly affect your long-term cost of ownership.</p>\n\n<h2>Why Work With Camelback Home Group</h2>\n<p>Buying directly from a builder is not the same as a typical resale transaction. Builder contracts are written to protect the builder, and they often include non-standard terms on deposits, closing timelines, and warranty remedies. At <strong>Camelback Home Group</strong>, every transaction has <strong>attorney and paralegal oversight</strong>, so your contract, disclosures, title commitment, and HOA documents are reviewed with a legal eye before you sign. We help you understand what you're agreeing to and negotiate where it counts.</p>\n\n<h2>Schedule Your Private Showing</h2>\n<p>Move-in-ready model homes on oversized lots don't come along often, and this one won't last. To tour 24266 W Atlantis Way or to ask about other new-construction opportunities in Buckeye and the West Valley, call Camelback Home Group at <strong>(480) 203-3039</strong> or reach out through our website. We'll set up a showing at your convenience and walk you through every step from offer to closing.</p>"
