    metaDescription: "9828 E Ironwood Drive in Scottsdale Ranch — a move-in ready 4-bed, 2.5-bath home with pool, new roof, and lakefront community amenities, listed at $1,350,000.",
    content: "<h2>A Scottsdale Ranch Gem — Updated and Move-In Ready</h2><p>Tucked inside one of Scottsdale's most sought-after lakefront communities, 9828 E Ironwood Drive is the kind of home that stops you in your tracks. This Spanish-style residence in Scottsdale Ranch has been thoughtfully updated while preserving the warm, timeless character that makes this neighborhood so special. With four bedrooms, two and a half bathrooms, and 2,656 square feet of living space, it offers the room and flexibility that families and entertainers alike are looking for — and at $1,350,000, it represents a compelling entry point into one of the most amenity-rich communities in the 85258 zip code.</p><p>Originally built in 1984, this home has been given a fresh lease on life with a <strong>brand-new roof and full exterior paint completed in 2026</strong>. That is not a minor detail — a new roof in the Arizona desert is a five-figure investment that a buyer will not have to think about for decades. Inside, updated flooring, refinished cabinets, and new lighting fixtures create a clean, contemporary feel throughout.</p><h2>Inside the Home</h2><p>The floor plan at 9828 E Ironwood Drive is designed for the way people actually live. Vaulted ceilings give the main living areas an open, airy feel, while the separation between the formal living room and the family room means you have dedicated spaces for both quiet evenings and lively gatherings.</p><p>The family room is the heart of this home — anchored by an <strong>updated fireplace</strong> and opening directly to the backyard through sliding doors. It is the kind of space where weekend mornings with coffee and Sunday football afternoons feel equally at home. The kitchen overlooks the pool through a large picture window, keeping you connected to the outdoor living space while you cook.</p><p>The spacious primary suite is a genuine retreat, featuring a large walk-in closet and direct patio access — step outside with your morning coffee without walking through the rest of the house. The primary bathroom includes a full bath with separate shower and tub, double vanity, and granite counters. Three additional bedrooms provide space for children, guests, or a dedicated home office.</p><h2>The Backyard — Your Private Desert Oasis</h2><p>If the interior is where you live, the backyard at 9828 E Ironwood Drive is where you escape. The centerpiece is a <strong>sparkling diving pool with a rock waterfall feature</strong> — the kind of backyard focal point that makes every weekend feel like a resort vacation. A covered patio provides shaded outdoor dining space, while a separate gazebo offers another spot to relax or entertain.</p><p>Mature landscaping surrounds the entire yard, creating privacy and a lush, established feel that new construction simply cannot replicate. In the cooler months — which in Scottsdale means roughly October through April — this backyard becomes the primary living space, and it is designed to deliver on that promise.</p><h2>Scottsdale Ranch — The Community</h2><p>Scottsdale Ranch is not just a neighborhood — it is a lifestyle. Developed in the 1980s and 1990s around a series of lakes, parks, and community facilities, Scottsdale Ranch has matured into one of the most desirable addresses in central Scottsdale.</p><p>Residents enjoy access to <strong>Lake Serena</strong>, a stocked lake perfect for catch-and-release fishing and lakeside walks. The community center sits on the waterfront and serves as the hub for events, gatherings, and HOA activities. Nearby parks, tennis facilities, and walking paths round out an amenity package that rivals much newer master-planned communities.</p><p>Location-wise, Scottsdale Ranch sits in the heart of the action — minutes from Scottsdale Quarter and Kierland Commons for shopping and dining, with easy access to the Loop 101 for commuting to employers throughout the Valley. The 85258 zip code consistently ranks among Scottsdale's most sought-after, and homes in Scottsdale Ranch benefit from that demand at resale.</p><h2>The Market Context</h2><p>At $1,350,000 and roughly $508 per square foot, this home sits in the sweet spot of the Scottsdale market — above the entry-level condos and townhomes, but well below the multi-million-dollar estates of North Scottsdale. For buyers seeking a <strong>move-in ready, updated single-family home with a pool in a premier community</strong>, this price point delivers genuine value relative to what comparable properties are fetching in neighboring areas like McCormick Ranch and Gainey Ranch.</p><p>The new roof is a significant differentiator. Many homes of this vintage in Scottsdale are approaching or past the point where roof replacement is needed, and that $15,000–$25,000 expense is something the next owner of this home will not face for years to come.</p><h2>See It for Yourself</h2><p>Homes like 9828 E Ironwood Drive, Scottsdale, AZ 85258 do not stay on the market long — updated properties in Scottsdale Ranch with pools and community amenities attract serious buyers quickly. If this listing has caught your eye, the best next step is to schedule a private showing.</p><p>At Camelback Home Group, every transaction includes attorney and paralegal oversight at no additional cost to you. That means the purchase contract, inspection negotiations, title review, and closing documents for a home like this will be handled with both real estate expertise and legal precision — giving you a level of protection that most brokerages simply do not offer.</p><p><strong>Call us at (480) 203-3039</strong> or <a href=\"/#contact\">reach out online</a> to schedule a showing or ask questions about this property.</p>"
